   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG111 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13451 · Decision 932/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 22/08/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">DTG111 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13451 · QĐ 932/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 22/08/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>- Read textbook and install software before coming to class<br><br>- Complete assignments in class, submit online thoughout LMS or Classroom platform.<br><br>- Access the course website (<a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/</a>) for up-to-date information and material of the course.<br><br>- Actively participate into class, review and comments to classmate works, ask instructor questions, bring into class everyday samples for references.<br><br>- Complete homework and other requirements by instructors<br><br>- Using laptop in class only for taking note, research and doing assignment purposes<br><br>- No talking, surfing, chatting, gaming, facebooking, using phone etc. while the teacher giving instruction.<br><br>- Present at least 80% class attendance in order to pass the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>- Read textbook and install software before coming to class<br><br>- Complete assignments in class, submit online thoughout LMS or Classroom platform.<br><br>- Access the course website (<a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/</a>) for up-to-date information and material of the course.<br><br>- Actively participate into class, review and comments to classmate works, ask instructor questions, bring into class everyday samples for references.<br><br>- Complete homework and other requirements by instructors<br><br>- Using laptop in class only for taking note, research and doing assignment purposes<br><br>- No talking, surfing, chatting, gaming, facebooking, using phone etc. while the teacher giving instruction.<br><br>- Present at least 80% class attendance in order to pass the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (27)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (27)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is a workspace? Why it's important to organize your workspace efficiently when using visual design tools.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>QN2</td><td>How to organize a workspace to suit specific tasks?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>QN3</td><td>How many main formats in which to store images in Illustrator. Why would you choose one over another, and what are the differences?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td>QN1</td><td>How to complete this artwork in the fastest way using Illustrator? (Artwork according to the lecturer's assignment.)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td>QN1</td><td>How to combine simple shapes to make more complex shapes?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td>QN2</td><td>What are the advantages of creating complex shapes from basic or geometric shapes?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td>QN1</td><td>How many ways to add text? What are the differences between the ways?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td>QN2</td><td>How to change type format and paragraphs format?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>QN1</td><td>How to add color to shapes and other vector objects in Adobe Illustrator?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>QN2</td><td>What are differences between Color panel and Swatches panel?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>QN1</td><td>What does mask mean in Adobe? What is the purpose of a mask in Illustrator?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>QN2</td><td>How many types of masks in illustrator?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the difference between RGB and CMYK color mode? How to convert RGB files to CMYK? And how to do the opposite in Photoshop?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>QN2</td><td>What is the resolution? When would you use a higher resolution and when would you use a lower resolution?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>QN3</td><td>What is bit depth? What does 8 bit depth mean?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the selection in Photoshop?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>QN2</td><td>What are the different selection tools in Photoshop and when would we use one of them?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>QN3</td><td>How to make a selection with the pen tool?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is a mask in Photoshop and why is it useful?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td>QN2</td><td>How to apply a layer mask?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>18</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is clone stamp tool? Which tool works similar to the clone stamp tool?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>22</td><td>QN1</td><td>How to set up a magazine file with 12 facing pages, 2.5 cm margins and 0.3 cm bleed?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>23</td><td>QN1</td><td>What are InDesign master pages and how to use it?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>25</td><td>QN1</td><td>What are the differences between the Frame tool and Rectangle tool in Adobe XD?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>26</td><td>QN1</td><td>What are components in Adobe XD? Why should you use components?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>26</td><td>QN2</td><td>What are Text style and Color Style in Adobe XD? Why should you use Text style and Color Style?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>27</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is Prototype?</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13451\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13451</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13451\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13451</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
